Backport of the adminType branch of epam/edp-keycloak-operator@817e77c (https://github.com/epam/edp-keycloak-operator/commit/817e77c29a417ee2d90f63a06e5fba5e176d3285): the keycloakv2 client ignores spec.adminType and always signs in with a password grant through admin-cli. With adminType serviceAccount the Secret holds a client ID and a client secret, so that sign-in fails, ClusterKeycloak reports connected: false, and every controller built on the keycloakv2 client (realms, groups, users, organizations) stops reconciling. The gocloak adapter the other controllers use already honours the field.

Applies to: epam/edp-keycloak-operator @ facbc36, pinned as COMMIT_REF in the Dockerfile one level up.

controller_helper_auth.go carries the same lines as the upstream commit, which also adds spec.auth around them; spec.auth is not backported. The test file is new: the upstream fake HTTP server answers every token request, so it cannot tell one grant from another.

Drop this file when COMMIT_REF moves past 817e77c.

